findings.comment:
4-602.13: The following non-food contact surfaces are observed soiled: 
KITCHEN: 1) back of the table by fryer/backing up to panini press and legs of same table;
                  2) circular fan is observed dusty - see that the fan is cleaned before being returned to use;
                  3) ceiling over the fry line is observed dusty (especially around air returns);
                  4) shelving within the cooler to the right of the hand sink (molded shelving);
DISH
                  1) top of dish machine soiled with food debris;
                  2) lime and scale accumulation within the dish machine;
                  3) the shelving in the walk-in cooler is observed coated in food and mold on shelving and wall around and behind the buttermilk;

STEAMTABLE: See that soiled water within basins is exchanged.

DRIVE-THRU: food debris is observed in the basin of the dough cooler. 

See that the aforementioned items are properly cleaned. 




 NonFOOD-CONTACT SURFACES of EQUIPMENT shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to preclude accumulation of soil residues.
